%description:

Tcp.fastopenClientEnabled:on -- host1 requests a cookie, and sends data on the next SYN.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open (RFC 7413), client: a connect() with fastOpen requests a cookie
from the server, and with a cached cookie it sends its first data on the SYN".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true, the value of LinuxTcp), and changed (the
parameter is @mutable). The code: TcpConnection::process_OPEN_ACTIVE() requests a cookie at a
connect() with fastOpen, or with a cached cookie lets the SYN wait for the first SEND, whose data
it carries; without Fast Open, the connect() is an ordinary one. This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, the client; host2 is a Fast Open server (precondition). host1 opens connection 1 at 0.1 s with Fast Open, which requests a cookie; at 0.5 s it opens
connection 2 with Fast Open and sends 500 bytes, which go on the SYN when host1 has a cookie
of host2. Observation: level 1, the SYN of connection 1 requests a cookie; the SYN of connection 2 carries
the cookie and the 500 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenClientEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenClientEnabledOn")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 1: a cookie request")
                  .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[1]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 2 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .capture("isn2", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie.size() == 16;
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 2, with 500 bytes and the cookie")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenClientEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenClientEnabledOn: PASS
